{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"aphidian-unartful-hound","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# The snapshot differ plans a phantom outbound update one pass after our own write\n\n## Symptom\n\n`tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_dc_mutations.py::test_a_repeat_pass_over_a_converged_pair_plans_nothing`\nfails against the live Jira Data Center harness (run 30724309686). After an outbound title edit\nhas demonstrably landed on the instance AND become visible to a JQL search, a scoped dry-run\nstill plans\n`{'direction':'outbound','action':'update','target':'RBJQFTF-1','local_id':'RBJQFTF-1'}`.\nIndex lag is excluded by construction (the cell waits for the search to reflect the new value).\n\n## Proven root cause\n\n`run_differs.py:222` calls `ctx.differ.compute_mutations(ctx.prev_snapshot, ctx.curr_snapshot)`,\nfeeding the PREVIOUS PASS'S REMOTE SNAPSHOT into the parameter `differ.py:5-11` defines as the\nLOCAL source-of-truth state — the legacy argument shape that same docstring says was replaced.\n\n`_compute_mutations_emit_both` (`differ.py:556-607`) then diffs every field outside\n`EXCLUDED_FIELDS = (\"local_id\",\"rebar-id\")` (`config.py:5`) and emits `(outbound, update)` with\n`changed[field] = local_val`, i.e. the STALE prev value, with provenance `local_id = target`\n(the Jira key) via `_derive_provenance` (`differ.py:130-131`) — the exact signature observed.\n\n`reconcile.py:613` advances the prev snapshot with `shutil.copy2(curr_path, prev_path)`, i.e.\nfrom the PRE-APPLY fetch, so an outbound write applied during pass N is invisible to `prev` at\npass N+1. One pass after our own write lands, prev != curr and the phantom is emitted. In a\ndry-run `persist` is False, so prev never advances and it is re-planned forever.\n\nReproduced locally with no Jira:\n\n    prev = {\"K-1\": {..., \"summary\": OLD, ...}}\n    curr = {\"K-1\": {..., \"summary\": NEW, ...}}\n    differ.compute_mutations(prev, curr)\n    -> outbound/update target=K-1 local_id=K-1 payload={\"summary\": OLD}\n    differ.compute_mutations(curr, curr) -> []\n\nThe mutation is inert at apply time: its payload is a bare field dict, not\n`{\"changed_fields\": ...}`, so `batch_dispatch._mutation_to_batch_dict:100-103` resolves\n`fields` to `{}` and `dispatch_one._update_one_scalar_update:640-650` issues an empty\n`update_issue(key)`. Nothing changes remotely, so the mutation can never be satisfied — planned\nevery pass, counted against the `BOOTSTRAP_STRICT` cap of 10 (`mode.py:104-111`), inflating\n`mutation_count` and making \"converged\" a lie.\n\nDo NOT remedy this by correcting the payload shape: that would make it apply, reverting every\nremote edit one pass later and flip-flopping forever.\n\n## Why this is a defect and not intended behaviour\n\n* `reconcile.py:609` states the invariant it breaks: \"Advance prev snapshot so the next call\n  converges to zero mutations.\"\n* `differ.py:80-92` and the label branch at `differ.py:576-582` are a CLOSED fix (ticket\n  robe-creek-zealot) for this exact mechanism, described verbatim there as a \"spurious\n  (outbound, update) echo\". It was applied to labels only; every other field still churns. This\n  bug is that fix's unswept sibling.\n* Story 26de's contract, `differ.py:688-691`: \"a write recorded as local-origin on pass N must\n  not re-emit on pass N+1 even if the jira snapshot has not yet caught up.\"\n\n## Blast radius\n\nOne cause explains all thirteen idempotence failures in harness run 30721408463, in BOTH\ndirections — the trigger is only \"the remote issue changed since the last persisted fetch\",\nindependent of which side changed it or which field.\n\n## Fix\n\nDrop the snapshot differ's field-drift `(outbound, update)` mutations at the\n`run_differs.py:222` call site, keyed on their provenance (`source=\"differ\"`,\n`reason=\"field_drift\"`). Do NOT change `differ.compute_mutations`'s documented local-vs-jira\ncontract: its unit tests legitimately exercise that contract with real local state, and other\ncallers may rely on it. For a bound pair, field sync in both directions is already owned by\n`_run_differs_outbound` / `_run_differs_inbound`, which run immediately afterwards, so the\nsnapshot differ's field-drift emission there is pure noise.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. A unit test drives the real diff phase with `prev` = a snapshot and `curr` = the same\n   snapshot with one field changed, and asserts NO outbound update is planned. The test is seen\n   RED before the fix and GREEN after, and returns to RED when the fix is reverted.\n2. A genuinely new key (present in `curr` only) still yields its `(inbound, create)` — the\n   edge-triggered inbound-create path the multi-page pagination cell depends on is unaffected.\n3. `make lint`, `make typecheck` and the reconciler unit/integration suites pass unchanged.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nFinding 6 of ticket 5200 (a deleted DC issue plans an outbound CREATE instead of an inbound\nprobe) comes from the SAME emitter — a key present in prev-but-not-curr is read as \"local has\nit, Jira does not\". It is a separate observable and is not fixed here.","id":"727f-b351-59ba-4b3b","parent_id":"e369-a449-4773-48fb","priority":1,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Snapshot differ plans a phantom outbound update after our own write"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785644844336334001,"uuid":"e5736387-e569-40ef-9d85-577015f55d4e"}